@@ -101,6 +101,8 @@ The shim defines `claude`, `pi`, `opencode`, `codex`, `devin` and `cursor-agent`
 - The arguments open an interactive session. Subcommands such as `claude doctor`, `codex exec` or `opencode run`, print modes such as `-p`, version and help run the binary directly. Each list comes from that runtime's own `--help`. Codex `resume` and `fork`, and Cursor `agent`, `ls` and `resume` stay wrapped, because they open a session.
 - A `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop` exists in the current directory or one of its parents. A `.skilled` that is a symlink counts, so the wrapper also starts in a repository that links this checkout's `.skilled`.
 
+The shim resolves only wrappers inside the sourced checkout, a linked worktree registered to it, or an absolute checkout listed in `SKILLED_LOOP_TRUSTED_CHECKOUTS` as a colon-separated value. An unset or empty variable trusts no extra checkout.
+
 The automatic hop in a linking repository also needs that repository's runtime folders, because each runtime reads its hooks or plugins from the project it starts in. Link `.claude`, `.codex`, `.opencode` and `.pi` from this checkout as well, or give each its own session-relaunch registration. A repository that links only `.skilled` starts under the wrapper but never receives the nudge, so its sessions hop only through `/speckit:handoff`.
 
 In every other case the function runs `command <binary> "$@"`. `skilled_loop_resolve <runtime> [args...]` prints the wrapper path the shim would use, or nothing. It skips the terminal check, so you can call it from a script to see the decision. Claude, Pi, OpenCode and Codex then hop on their own near the context threshold. Cursor and Devin run under the wrapper too, but they hop only after `/speckit:handoff`, as section 1 describes. An alias with the same name still takes precedence over the function, so remove a `claude` alias before you rely on the shim. Agent tool shells, such as Claude Code's, are rebuilt from a function snapshot that drops names starting with a single underscore, so every helper the shim's functions call keeps a plain `skilled_loop_` name.
